$"Usage:  KNEW infile [outfile] [options]"#10"  where infile  - KAREL file to b"
"e converted."#10"        outfile - Optional output file name.  If omitted, inp"
"ut file will"#10"                  be renamed 'infile.BK' and output will be '"
"infile.KL'."#10"        options - One or more of the following:"#10"          "
"      /b - Build library file.  Used after converting with the /m"#10"        "
"             option.  'infile' must be the same name as 'progname'"#10"       "
"              used by the /m switch."#10"                /i - Do not convert i"
"nclude files.  They are normally con-"#10"                     verted as they "
"are encountered.  Always set if 'outfile'"#10"                     is specifie"
"d."#10"                /l[=listfile] - List screen output to 'listfile'.  If n"
"o file"#10"                     name is provided, 'infile.LS' is used."#10"   "
"             /m[=progname] - Multi-module mode.  'progname' is the name of"#10
"                     the program 'infile' is called from.  If 'progname' is"
#10"                     omitted, 'infile' is used as the program name."#10"   "
"             /t - Suppress file output to screen."#10#10$"Too many files open,"
